	     Building and Installing Emacs from the Repository

The Emacs repository is hosted on Savannah.  The following Git command
will clone the repository to the 'emacs' subdirectory of the current
directory on your local machine:

    git clone https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/emacs.git

* On this fork (claude/migrate-to-meson-ninja-ZSbvG) the autotools
  entry points (configure.ac, autogen.sh, every Makefile.in,
  GNUmakefile, make-dist) have been removed; Meson + Ninja is the
  only supported build system.  See
  .claude/plans/migrate-from-current-build-replicated-gadget.md for
  history.

* Quick start:

    meson setup build -Dnative-compilation=yes
    meson compile -C build              # builds emacs + emacs.pdmp
    meson test -C build --suite smoke   # ERT smoke tests
    meson install -C build --destdir=/tmp/stage

* Build dependencies (Debian / Ubuntu names):

    meson, ninja-build, python3, pkg-config, gcc, libc6-dev,
    libgtk-3-dev, libcairo2-dev, libpango1.0-dev, libharfbuzz-dev,
    libfreetype-dev, libfontconfig1-dev, libxft-dev, libgnutls28-dev,
    libtree-sitter-dev, libsqlite3-dev, libxml2-dev, libsystemd-dev,
    libgmp-dev, libgccjit-13-dev, libjansson-dev, libncurses-dev,
    libacl1-dev, libjpeg-dev, libtiff-dev, libgif-dev, libpng-dev,
    librsvg2-dev, libwebp-dev, liblcms2-dev, libdbus-1-dev,
    zlib1g-dev, plus the X11 stack (libx11-dev, libxfixes-dev,
    libxrender-dev, libxrandr-dev, libxcomposite-dev,
    libxinerama-dev, libxi-dev, libxext-dev, libxtst-dev, libsm-dev,
    libice-dev, libtinfo-dev), texinfo, gawk.

* Out-of-tree builds: every meson setup is automatically out-of-tree;
  the build directory you pass to `meson setup` need not be inside
  the source tree.

* Cross-compiling: see cross/meson-android.cross and
  cross/meson-macos.cross.  Pass them with --cross-file.

* devenv (Nix): for a pinned local toolchain, `devenv shell` enters a
  Nix-pinned environment; the same packages are listed for apt above.

* For a small set of dependencies, see admin/quick-install-emacs and
  the meson_install.py script under meson/.
